From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:17:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: MT7986 SoC bring-up, DMA setup, EEPROM and
 register access

101 KUnit tests in 5 suites. In-scope coverage:
- mt7915/soc.c: 0% -> 87.6%
- mt7915/dma.c: 0% -> 99.2%
- mt7915/eeprom.c: 0% -> 93.9%
- eeprom.c: 0% -> 92.9%
- mt7915/mmio.c: 46.6% -> 93.7%

- mt7915-soc: both A-dies are modelled behind the SPI bridge.
  - SPI access and timeouts, efuse reads, thermal calibration;
  - crystal trims and patches for the 7975 and 7976;
  - A-die config, AFE calibration, SKU setup and update;
  - PLL, clocks, bus timeouts and WiFi subsystem power-up;
  - pin states, enable and disable;
  - the probe and init error paths.
- mt7915-dma:
  - the MT7986 queue layout and prefetch split;
  - full DMA setup with the ring registers checked, band 1's tx ring
    included;
  - non-forced and forced reset.
- mt7915-eeprom:
  - efuse loading through the fake firmware, and loading from the device
    tree;
  - the chip id check and default files;
  - precal, band config, hardware caps, target power and power delta.
- mt76-eeprom, with a device tree built in memory:
  - DT data, MTD and NVMEM sources, and the MAC override;
  - power-limit nodes, stream deltas and backoff tables, and
    mt76_get_rate_power_limits().
- mt7915-mmio:
  - each chip's register layout and L1/L2 windows;
  - the interrupt tasklet and handler, rx poll, and the dual-interface
    mask.

Six tests are skipped. Each one shows a suspected driver bug:
- mt7915_mmio_init() reads MT_HW_REV before mdev->rev is set, so probing
  the MT7986 does an L2-remap read-modify-write with the MT7916 layout
  (window offset 0x1b8, TOP_RGU+0x1b8).
- Thermal calibration writes its trims even when the efuse read fails.
- The MT7976 crystal strap mode is decoded with FIELD_PREP instead of
  FIELD_GET, so 40 MHz crystals are never trimmed.
- The MT7975 XO_CTRL2 trim value is always 0 (FIELD_GET of the C1/C2
  masks on a 7-bit trim).
- mt798x_wmac_sku_setup() returns 0 when the A-die chip id read fails,
  and enable goes on with an uninitialised adie_type.
- mt76_eeprom_init() turns -EPROBE_DEFER from the NVMEM cell into "no
  EEPROM in the device tree", and falls back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
